The pixel shaders carry the emulated path's ucode hash (HashShaderUcode, the XXH3 of the microcode as Xenia hashes
it); the draw overrides keyed by it (burstlimit_patches.cpp: depth_of_field, glow_blur, motion_blur, soft_filter)
drop the draws or replace pixel constants, so the background is as sharp as on the emulated path. Diagnostics, only
with banjo_renut_diag_draw_log_s: the logged draws name the pixel shader c255 (device, literal, upload) and the
toon shaders' c0-c8; the 256x256 DXT1 ramps and wide DXT5 textures log their first blocks once ([db-ramp]).

